          <div class="li-faq-item"><h3>3. Who is this service for?</h3><div>Founders, CEOs, MDs, professional managers, banking + financial services professionals, real estate developers, B2B manufacturing leaders, consulting partners, SaaS founders, and senior executives across India + GCC who use LinkedIn as their primary channel but lack an in-house LinkedIn team.</div></div>
          <div class="li-faq-item"><h3>4. Which cities does ITD serve?</h3><div>India: Mumbai, Delhi NCR, Bangalore, Hyderabad, Pune, Chennai, Ahmedabad, Kolkata. GCC: Dubai, Abu Dhabi, Riyadh, Jeddah, Doha, Kuwait City, Manama, Muscat. Remote onboarding + service delivery across all locations.</div></div>
          <div class="li-faq-item"><h3>5. How does the ghostwriting process work?</h3><div>Six-step voice-capture: (1) 60-min structured interview capturing your vocabulary + opinions + writing patterns, (2) Weekly 15-min brief calls for fresh material, (3) Writer drafts from your voice-captured content, (4) You review + approve via shared doc/WhatsApp with 24-48hr SLA, (5) We publish on schedule + monitor comments/DMs, (6) Continuous voice refinement. Content sounds authentically you &mdash; because it IS your voice + insight.</div></div>
          <div class="li-faq-item"><h3>6. How can I select a package?</h3><div>Use the package selection form on this page &mdash; pick Starter, Growth, Premium, or Enterprise from the dropdown + fill in name + email + mobile + role. Your selection reaches the ITD team via email + WhatsApp. We respond within 24 hours with a scoped proposal + 90-day plan.</div></div>
          <div class="li-faq-item"><h3>7. Can I switch packages later?</h3><div>Yes. Standard practice is to start at Starter or Growth for 3-6 months, then upgrade to Premium or Enterprise as your goals + content velocity + inbound scale. Downgrades also allowed month-to-month after your initial 6-month MSA.</div></div>
          <div class="li-faq-item"><h3>8. What compliance issues apply for banking professionals?</h3><div>SEBI + RBI + AMFI advertising norms + firm compliance. Practically: no product-specific promises, no return-guarantee language, all specific-instrument commentary with risk disclosure + disclaimer, client-stories anonymised or with written consent + firm approval, AMFI/IRDAI-compliant mutual fund + insurance content. ITD compliance advisor reviews every post pre-publish.</div></div>
          <div class="li-faq-item"><h3>9. What content works best for a real estate developer or broker?</h3><div>Market outlook + micro-market analysis (30%), project launches + commercial-leasing wins with client permission (25%), RERA + regulatory updates (15%), industry-body (REDCO/NAREDCO/CREDAI) engagement + speaking (15%), market data with commentary (15%). Video project + drone tours drive 3-5x engagement.</div></div>
          <div class="li-faq-item"><h3>10. What content works best for B2B manufacturing MDs?</h3><div>Product + technical deep-dives with drawings/CAD/videos (30-35%), plant + quality + certification content (20-25%), export success stories + trade-show recap (15-20%), industry regulation + Aatmanirbhar Bharat updates (10-15%), team + hiring (10-15%). Video content is manufacturing's LinkedIn superpower.</div></div>
          <div class="li-faq-item"><h3>11. What content works best for founders/CEOs of SaaS/tech companies?</h3><div>Product marketing thought leadership (30-35%), growth-metric transparency (20-25%), hiring + team + culture (15-20%), customer stories + PLG frameworks (10-15%), industry commentary + long-form essays (10-15%). India SaaS founder community has shifted to metric-transparency + LinkedIn newsletter dominance.</div></div>
          <div class="li-faq-item"><h3>12. How long before we see meaningful results?</h3><div>Month 1-3: baseline (300-1,000 new followers, first inbound DMs). Month 3-6: acceleration (1,500-4,000 followers, first booked meetings from LinkedIn). Month 6-12: consistent inbound (5,000-15,000 followers, 20-80 qualified DMs/month, 5-30 booked meetings/month). Month 12+: compounding, LinkedIn becomes primary top-of-funnel.</div></div>
          <div class="li-faq-item"><h3>13. Does ITD run Sales Navigator + InMail outreach?</h3><div>Yes at Growth tier and above. We build ICP lists via Sales Navigator (Rs 5,000-8,000/month per seat), send personalised connection requests + InMail sequences (proven templates + industry-native writing), and hand qualified leads to your sales team. Typical response rate 15-35% for well-crafted sequences.</div></div>
          <div class="li-faq-item"><h3>14. Does ITD run LinkedIn Ads?</h3><div>Yes at Premium and Enterprise tiers. Sponsored Content + Message Ads + Conversation Ads + Lead Gen Forms + Retargeting. Meta CAPI-equivalent LinkedIn Conversions API + LTV-weighted bidding + weekly performance review. Ad spend separate + transparent pass-through (no markup).</div></div>
          <div class="li-faq-item"><h3>15. What's your contract structure?</h3><div>6-month Master Service Agreement (MSA) with cancellation option after month 3 if agreed milestones not met &mdash; protects both sides. Monthly retainer + agreed deliverables. Ad-spend transparent pass-through (no markup). IP ownership 100% client on creative + content library + attribution + WhatsApp automation. Notice period 30-60 days.</div></div>
          <div class="li-faq-item"><h3>16. Can I share LinkedIn account access, or should ITD manage from a shared login?</h3><div>Two options: (1) You add ITD as Company Page admin + Sales Nav team seat (for Sales Nav + Company Page), and post approved content from your own account through us or via LinkedIn's scheduling tools, or (2) You provide account access via password manager (LastPass/1Password shared vault). Option 1 preferred for enterprise + compliance-sensitive clients.</div></div>
          <div class="li-faq-item"><h3>17. How does approval + publish workflow work?</h3><div>ITD writer drafts → shared Google Doc or WhatsApp with attachments + supporting research. You review + approve or request edits within agreed 24-48hr SLA. ITD publishes on approved schedule + monitors comments/DMs + escalates compliance-adjacent DMs to you. Firm compliance officer can be included in workflow for regulated roles.</div></div>
          <div class="li-faq-item"><h3>18. What KPIs do you report on?</h3><div>Weekly: profile views + connection acceptance + follower growth + post engagement + inbound DMs + saved content + newsletter subscribers. Monthly: qualified inbound DMs + booked meetings + LinkedIn-attributed hires/customers/deals + brand-search lift. Quarterly: cohort attribution + LinkedIn-attributed revenue + long-term LTV.</div></div>
